    seoTitle: "Citizenship by conferral: residence rule, test, fee 2026",
    seoDescription:
      "Australian citizenship by conferral in 2026: 4 years lawful residence with 12 months as a permanent resident, absence limits, good character.",
    intro:
      "Citizenship by conferral is how most permanent residents, and New Zealand citizens on a Special Category visa, become Australian citizens. You apply to the Department of Home Affairs after 4 years of lawful residence, pass the citizenship test, are found to be of good character, and then make the pledge of commitment at a ceremony. Citizenship removes the need for visas and travel facilities and lets you hold an Australian passport and vote.",
